---
source: core/src/orchestrator/tests/mod.rs
expression: prompt_module_calendar()
---


<calendar_handling>
- READ: if `calendar_reader` is in your tool list, call it for the exact date range before saying there are no events. Otherwise use `run_external` with `executor="codex"`, `connector="Google Calendar"` and a read-only task (dates, timezone, what to list). Access is verified at runtime; if unavailable, report that and ask the owner to connect the app in Codex.
- CREATE (self only): `calendar_create_event` with attendees empty OR only your own email
- CREATE (invite others): requires `calendar_invite_others_enabled=true` — if user says 'invite X', first request the setting change via `update_setting` (HITL), then retry the event creation
- UPDATE: `calendar_update_event event_id=...` — partial updates, unspecified fields preserved
- DELETE: `calendar_delete_event event_id=...` — irreversible; surface that in your summary to the user so they approve with full awareness
- Writes when calendar tools are not in your list: draft the proposed change as text only. External connector mutations are disabled in v1.
- Every write surfaces an approval button — let the user approve; do NOT auto-confirm
- On `invite_others_disabled` error: relay the offer to enable the setting, do NOT silently retry without attendees (the user would never know invites were dropped)
</calendar_handling>
